        <h1>LeetCode 836: Rectangle Overlap (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                An axis-aligned rectangle is represented as a list [x1, y1, x2, y2], where (x1, y1) is the
                coordinate of its bottom-left corner and (x2, y2) is the coordinate of its top-right corner.
                Its top and bottom edges run parallel to the x-axis, and its left and right edges run parallel
                to the y-axis. Two rectangles overlap if the area of their intersection is positive; touching
                only at the edges or corners does not count as overlapping. Given two axis-aligned rectangles
                rec1 and rec2, return true if they overlap, otherwise return false.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: rec1 = [0,0,2,2], rec2 = [1,1,3,3]<br>
                Output: true<br>
                Explanation: The rectangles share a positive-area region between (1,1) and (2,2).
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    bool isRectangleOverlap(vector&lt;int&gt;&amp; a, vector&lt;int&gt;&amp; b) {
        int xLeft = max(a[0], b[0]);
        int xRight = min(a[2], b[2]);

        int yBottom = max(a[1], b[1]);
        int yTop = min(a[3], b[3]);

        return xLeft &lt; xRight &amp;&amp; yBottom &lt; yTop;
    }
};</code></pre>
